# 24GB+ VRAM profile -- development boxes and enthusiast hardware.
#
# The quality tier. Illustrious XL rather than SD1.5, because Spike 0 showed the
# failures were prompt adherence -- outfit, pose and framing tags being ignored --
# not character consistency, and Illustrious is markedly better at exactly that.
#
# Budget at peak. File sizes are verified; VRAM figures are ESTIMATES and the image
# side in particular has not been measured yet.
#   Illustrious XL v2.0            ~7.0 GB   (verified file size)
#   + ControlNet OpenPose SDXL     ~2.5 GB   (verified file size)
#   + IP-Adapter Plus + ViT-H      ~3.4 GB   (verified file size)
#   + activations @ 1024px         ~1.5 GB   (estimate)
#   Gemma 4 12B QAT q4_0           ~7.0 GB   (verified file size)
#     + 32k KV cache               ~1.5 GB   (estimate)
#   --------------------------------------
#   total                         ~23 GB
#
# That is over 24 GB once fragmentation is counted, so this profile realistically
# wants 32 GB, or a smaller LLM, or ComfyUI's own offloading to do the work. Measure
# before trusting it. Gemma 4 26B-A4B (14.4 GB) does not fit alongside this at all.
#
# This profile deliberately does NOT share a style pack with the 12GB one. A pack is
# locked per save (HANDOFF 1.5), so a save made here cannot be opened on a 12 GB box.

# Rolling tag. A dated tag (cu130-slim-YYYYMMDD) pins the stack instead, at the cost
# of not picking up ComfyUI updates; swap it in if a future upgrade breaks generation.
#
# cu130 is required here, not merely preferred. On an RTX 5090 the cu126 image
# starts and reports the device correctly, then fails every kernel launch with
# "no kernel image is available for execution on the device" -- its PyTorch has no
# sm_120 kernels compiled in. cu124 does not support Blackwell at all.
COMFY_IMAGE=yanwk/comfyui-boot:cu130-slim
COMFY_PORT=8188
# --highvram keeps models in VRAM between runs instead of evicting them.
#
# Measured without it on a 32GB card: ComfyUI dumped the ControlNet and IP-Adapter
# after every generation and re-read them from the bind mount at ~24 s/GB, so a sprite
# cost 148s against 8s for the same checkpoint with no adapters. Roughly 140s of that
# was disk, not compute. Its memory estimator is far too conservative here -- 23GB was
# free throughout.
COMFY_EXTRA_ARGS=--highvram

MODELS_PATH=./models
CUSTOM_NODES_PATH=./custom_nodes
OUTPUT_PATH=./output
INPUT_PATH=./input

LLM_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-cuda
LLM_PORT=8080
LLM_HF_REPO=google/gemma-4-12B-it-qat-q4_0-gguf
LLM_HF_FILE=gemma-4-12b-it-qat-q4_0.gguf
LLM_CTX=32768
LLM_GPU_LAYERS=999
LLM_ALIAS=chat

EMBEDDINGS_PORT=8081
EMBEDDINGS_HF_REPO=nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v1.5-GGUF
EMBEDDINGS_HF_FILE=nomic-embed-text-v1.5.Q8_0.gguf
EMBEDDINGS_CTX=2048
EMBEDDINGS_GPU_LAYERS=999
EMBEDDINGS_ALIAS=embeddings

IPADAPTER_REF=main

# Both model sets: SD1.5 stays available for comparison against Illustrious.
MANIFESTS=models-sd15.tsv models-sdxl.tsv
INSTALL_CONTROLNET_AUX=1

# --- Checkpoint evaluation (optional) ---------------------------------------
# Uncomment to pull the candidates in docs/model-evaluation.md. ~29 GB, and not
# needed to run the game. INSTALL_EXTRA_MODELS is Sana only: ComfyUI has no
# native Sana nodes, so it needs a third-party node pack in-process.
#
# MANIFESTS=models-sd15.tsv models-sdxl.tsv models-eval.tsv
# INSTALL_EXTRA_MODELS=1
